    "q-127852": {
      "dom_id": "step-q127852",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The vector $u$ has magnitude $5$, the vector $v$ has magnitude $4,$ the angle between $u$ and $v$ is ${160}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $u\\times v.$ Find $u\\times v$ in terms of $n.$ Round your final answer to one decimal place where appropriate.",
      "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{160}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =20\\cdot (0.342\\,02…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(6.840\\,40…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈6.8n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
